  "id": "DrugBank_DB00741 - MONDO_5062",
  "verbalization": "Hydrocortisone is implicated in the development of lymphoma through a shared pathway involving dexamethasone, a corticosteroid. The evidence suggests that Hydrocortisone, through its indication for diseases such as Orbital Region Disease and Musculoskeletal System Disease, leads to the use of dexamethasone, which in turn is associated with lymphoma. This indicates a potential mechanism where corticosteroids, through their anti-inflammatory and immunosuppressive effects, may contribute to the progression of lymphoma. The presence of multiple indirect pathways linking Hydrocortisone to dexamethasone and ultimately to lymphoma highlights a possible role of corticosteroids in the pathogenesis of lymphoma, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of corticosteroids in the context of lymphoma, suggesting a broader therapeutic or prognostic significance.",
